ap throughput to/from node2 (10.100.237.11) at ~1Mbit/s in each direction, while leaving node1's other traffic (e.g. to node3) unshaped. Egress shaping uses an HTB class filtered on dst=node2's IP on br-lan; ingress shaping redirects src=node2 traffic to an IFB device with a matching 1mbit HTB class. Config persisted via a new /etc/init.d/tc-node2-shape boot script (S99/K10). Demonstrated the limit with real 8MB SCP transfers between node2 and node1 in both directions (~70.4s each ≈ 0.95Mbit/s), and proved node1's traffic to node3 is unaffected (a 300-packet/1400B ping burst to node3 completed in ~10ms, routed through the unshaped default HTB class with zero overlimits, vs. class 1:10 for node2 which showed overlimit throttling). Completed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol: captured boot_id baselines on all three nodes, restarted each one at a time (node1 then node2 then node3) via native reboot, confirmed boot_id changed after each restart, and verified recovery (tc shaping/ifb/dropbear alive on node1; network/services active and repeat SCP test still shaped correctly on node2; sshd active on node3). All temporary test files and injected SSH keys were cleaned up afterward.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology: node1=OpenWrt 25.12.2 (single br-lan/eth0 on 10.100.237.0/24), node2 & node3=RHEL7 hosts on the same subnet\",\"Installed tc-full, kmod-ifb, kmod-sched-act-police on node1 via apk\",\"Configured HTB egress shaping on br-lan: default class 1:1 (1Gbit, unshaped) + class 1:10 (1mbit) filtered on dst=node2\",\"Configured HTB ingress shaping via ifb0: qdisc ingress on br-lan redirects src=node2 traffic to ifb0, where class 1:10 (1mbit) rate-limits it\",\"Wrote and enabled /etc/init.d/tc-node2-shape boot script implementing the above, verified start/stop/restart idempotency\",\"Set up temporary SSH key trust (cluster keypair) between node2->node1 and node1->node3 for transfer testing\",\"Ran 8MB SCP transfers node2<->node1 in both directions, timing ~70.4s each (~0.95Mbit/s), matching the 1Mbit/s target\",\"Ran a 300-packet/1400B ping burst from node1 to node3 and inspected tc -s class counters to prove node1's non-node2 traffic uses the unshaped default class\",\"Captured boot_id/uptime baseline on node1, node2, node3\",\"Restarted node1, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, verified tc shaping/ifb/dropbear survived reboot, re-ran SCP test confirming shaping persisted\",\"Restarted node2, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, verified network/services and re-ran SCP test confirming shaping still enforced\",\"Restarted node3, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, verified sshd active and networking restored\",\"Cleaned up test files and temporary SSH keys/authorized_keys entries on all three nodes\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 shaping config (HTB egress class for node2, 1mbit)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-53c9a819554b4911\"],\"summary\":\"tc qdisc/class/filter show confirms 1:10 class capped at 1Mbit filtered on dst 10.100.237.11 (0a64ed0b hex = node2 IP), default class 1:1 at 1Gbit\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 ingress shaping config (IFB redirect + HTB for node2 traffic inbound)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-891e653033c64cf5\"],\"summary\":\"ifb0 created, HTB 1:10 class capped at 1Mbit filtered on src 10.100.237.11, br-lan ingress qdisc redirects matching src traffic to ifb0\"},{\"requirement\":\"Shaping persists via boot-time service (init script)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1ec1d057cda54e38\",\"cmd-c55f95d0e9594ec0\"],\"summary\":\"Created /etc/init.d/tc-node2-shape, enabled for boot (S99/K10 symlinks), verified stop/start cycle correctly tears down and rebuilds shaping\"},{\"requirement\":\"Demonstrate ~1Mbit/s limit with a measured transfer (node2->node1 and node1->node2)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-712a58cb7f6d4f42\",\"cmd-7a2755911e614fa3\"],\"summary\":\"8MB (8388608 byte) SCP transfers each took ~70.4s in both directions = ~953 kbit/s, matching the ~1Mbit/s target\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1's own/other traffic (to node3) remains unshaped\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d76e2171657e4720\",\"cmd-8d3294729d0a4bd3\"],\"summary\":\"300-packet 1400B ping burst node1->node3 completed in 0.01s (~338Mbit/s) and tc -s class show attributes it to the unshaped default class 1:1 with zero overlimits, distinct from the throttled node2 class 1:10\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart: healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-42f9b21dbe9844c6\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id ffbc2777-7df8-490e-9496-ec4de44d03e8 and confirmed tc shaping/ifb0/filters active prior to reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart: acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9f0aeec47ee04ba1\"],\"summary\":\"reboot command executed in background; SSH connection closed by remote host confirming reboot was issued\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart: changed boot identity confirmed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a34ccb654a064b63\"],\"summary\":\"New boot_id 82cbbcf5-ff6b-4d10-9f87-7a093c3b97ea differs from baseline, confirming actual restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart: recovered state verified\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-621ac3d65db248a3\",\"cmd-a5953b892e7148d6\"],\"summary\":\"Post-reboot tc qdisc/class/ifb0/filters all restored automatically via init script; repeat SCP transfer still took ~70.3s confirming shaping re-applied correctly\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node2 restart: healthy baseline before restart (incl. data integrity)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9ac72249a3ba4f06\",\"cmd-d12f9954c59d4cc0\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 9294b73f-ae6b-465c-9de5-9f2821107555; verified matching md5sums between original and downloaded test file proving data integrity before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node2 restart: acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-71c94a50d99d4043\"],\"summary\":\"sudo reboot executed in background; connection closed by remote host confirming reboot issued\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node2 restart: cha