dropbear alive on node1; network/services active and repeat SCP test still shaped correctly on node2; sshd active on node3). All temporary test files and injected SSH keys were cleaned up afterward.","actions_performed":["Surveyed topology: node1=OpenWrt 25.12.2 (single br-lan/eth0 on 10.100.237.0/24), node2 & node3=RHEL7 hosts on the same subnet","Installed tc-full, kmod-ifb, kmod-sched-act-police on node1 via apk","Configured HTB egress shaping on br-lan: default class 1:1 (1Gbit, unshaped) + class 1:10 (1mbit) filtered on dst=node2","Configured HTB ingress shaping via ifb0: qdisc ingress on br-lan redirects src=node2 traffic to ifb0, where class 1:10 (1mbit) rate-limits it","Wrote and enabled /etc/init.d/tc-node2-shape boot script implementing the above, verified start/stop/restart idempotency","Set up temporary SSH key trust (cluster keypair) between node2->node1 and node1->node3 for transfer testing","Ran 8MB SCP transfers node2<->node1 in both directions, timing ~70.4s each (~0.95Mbit/s), matching the 1Mbit/s target","Ran a 300-packet/1400B ping burst from node1 to node3 and inspected tc -s class counters to prove node1's non-node2 traffic uses the unshaped default class","Captured boot_id/uptime baseline on node1, node2, node3","Restarted node1, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, verified tc shaping/ifb/dropbear survived reboot, re-ran SCP test confirming shaping persisted","Restarted node2, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, verified network/services and re-ran SCP test confirming shaping still enforced","Restarted node3, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, verified sshd active and networking restored","Cleaned up test files and temporary SSH keys/authorized_keys entries on all three nodes"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 shaping config (HTB egress class for node2, 1mbit)","command_ids":["cmd-53c9a819554b4911"],"summary":"tc qdisc/class/filter show confirms 1:10 class capped at 1Mbit filtered on dst 10.100